    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4ed91397",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a plane taking off at sunset, with text overlay that reads: \"look at the plane, it's your uncle samir\" and \"*was\". The visual of the plane ascending is juxtaposed with the text to imply that the person named 'Samir' (likely of Middle Eastern or Muslim origin, given the name) is no longer alive or present, as if he was 'taken' by the plane. This is a darkly humorous or sarcastic meme that uses the image of a plane to symbolize death or disappearance, possibly referencing a tragic event involving a person named Samir. The intent is to create a punchline through the contrast between the grandeur of the plane taking off and the somber implication of death. There is no direct targeting of any protected group based on race, religion, gender, or sexual orientation in the text or image. The meme is not abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic. It is a form of dark humor or satire, using the visual metaphor of a plane to convey a tragic or ironic message. The overall intent is to evoke a sense of dark humor or irony by juxtaposing the image of a plane taking off with the implication of death or disappearance.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22336278"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
