      "instance_name": "mapping_001",
      "label": "Plane as Uncle Samir",
      "description": "The top text 'look at the plane, it's your uncle samir' explicitly maps the visual entity 'airplane' to the textual entity 'uncle samir'. This is an analogical mapping where the airplane is metaphorically identified as the person named 'Samir', implying his death or disappearance. The visual material (airplane) is being mapped onto the textual material (uncle samir) to create a darkly humorous or ironic statement.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
